1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:05,120
Negative exponents. A negative power is not a negative

2
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:08,222
number: it is a reciprocal. Let us see where

3
00:00:08,222 --> 00:00:09,531
the minus sign really goes.

4
00:00:10,087 --> 00:00:13,191
Last time, exponents wrote the Sun's width as one

5
00:00:13,191 --> 00:00:16,347
point four times ten to the power nine. Now

6
00:00:16,347 --> 00:00:19,793
look at something tiny: a human hair is about

7
00:00:19,793 --> 00:00:22,934
zero point zero zero zero zero zero five metres

8
00:00:22,934 --> 00:00:26,802
thick. Can exponents take us below one? We need

9
00:00:26,802 --> 00:00:28,318
a new kind of power.

10
00:00:28,867 --> 00:00:32,307
Start with the powers you already know. Ten cubed

11
00:00:32,307 --> 00:00:35,927
is one thousand. Divide by ten and the exponent

12
00:00:35,927 --> 00:00:39,467
drops to two: one hundred. Divide by ten again:

13
00:00:39,467 --> 00:00:41,441
ten to the power one is ten. And ten

14
00:00:41,441 --> 00:00:44,387
to the power zero is one. Every step down

15
00:00:44,387 --> 00:00:46,038
divides the value by ten.

16
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:49,520
But the staircase does not stop at one. Keep

17
00:00:49,520 --> 00:00:51,890
the same rule: one divided by ten is one

18
00:00:51,890 --> 00:00:54,211
tenth, so ten to the power minus one. One

19
00:00:54,211 --> 00:00:57,800
tenth divided by ten is one hundredth: ten to

20
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:00,748
the power minus two. And one thousandth is ten

21
00:01:00,748 --> 00:01:03,637
to the power minus three. The minus sign moves

22
00:01:03,637 --> 00:01:05,251
the power under one.

23
00:01:05,860 --> 00:01:09,008
The pattern is not special to ten. Try the

24
00:01:09,008 --> 00:01:13,900
base two: eight, four, two, one. Each step divides

25
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:16,845
by two. So one divided by two is one

26
00:01:16,845 --> 00:01:20,595
half: two to the power minus one. And one

27
00:01:20,595 --> 00:01:23,251
quarter is two to the power minus two.

28
00:01:23,797 --> 00:01:26,177
Now we can write the rule for any base

29
00:01:26,177 --> 00:01:29,377
a that is not zero. A raised to the

30
00:01:29,377 --> 00:01:32,917
power minus m equals one over a to the

31
00:01:32,917 --> 00:01:37,952
power m. The exponent becomes positive in the denominator,

32
00:01:37,952 --> 00:01:41,504
and the minus sign disappears. Read it the other

33
00:01:41,504 --> 00:01:43,777
way too: one over a to the power m

34
00:01:43,777 --> 00:01:46,068
equals a to the power minus m.

35
00:01:46,764 --> 00:01:49,747
Here is the mistake to avoid. Two to the

36
00:01:49,747 --> 00:01:52,151
power minus three is one over two cubed, which

37
00:01:52,151 --> 00:01:56,713
is one eighth, a positive fraction. But minus two

38
00:01:56,713 --> 00:02:00,584
cubed means minus eight. They are not equal. The

39
00:02:00,584 --> 00:02:04,835
minus sign belongs to the exponent, so it takes the reciprocal.

40
00:02:05,468 --> 00:02:07,658
Now look in a mirror. On the left, two

41
00:02:07,658 --> 00:02:10,468
cubed is eight. On the right, two to the

42
00:02:10,468 --> 00:02:13,508
power minus three is one eighth. Multiply them: eight

43
00:02:13,508 --> 00:02:16,828
times one eighth is one. In general, a to

44
00:02:16,828 --> 00:02:20,868
the power m times a to the power minus

45
00:02:20,868 --> 00:02:23,608
m is a to the power zero, which is

46
00:02:23,608 --> 00:02:28,699
one. So each is the multiplicative inverse of the other.

47
00:02:29,318 --> 00:02:31,929
Finding an inverse is quick. Three to the power

48
00:02:31,929 --> 00:02:34,238
minus five pairs with three to the power five,

49
00:02:34,238 --> 00:02:37,818
because their product is one. Four to the power

50
00:02:37,818 --> 00:02:40,538
minus three pairs with four cubed. And x to

51
00:02:40,538 --> 00:02:43,370
the power minus n pairs with x to the

52
00:02:43,370 --> 00:02:46,728
power n. The inverse of any power simply flips

53
00:02:46,728 --> 00:02:48,869
the sign of its exponent.

54
00:02:49,484 --> 00:02:52,284
Your turn. Three questions. Write ten to the power

55
00:02:52,284 --> 00:02:56,364
minus four with a positive exponent. Find the value

56
00:02:56,364 --> 00:02:59,644
of five to the power minus two. Write the

57
00:02:59,644 --> 00:03:03,435
multiplicative inverse of seven to the power minus three.

58
00:03:14,555 --> 00:03:16,709
Ten to the power minus four is one over

59
00:03:16,709 --> 00:03:20,515
ten to the power four: one over ten thousand.

60
00:03:20,515 --> 00:03:23,255
Five to the power minus two is one over

61
00:03:23,255 --> 00:03:26,975
five squared: one twenty fifth. And the inverse of

62
00:03:26,975 --> 00:03:30,166
seven to the power minus three is seven cubed.

63
00:03:30,809 --> 00:03:33,149
One last look. When the exponent goes down by

64
00:03:33,149 --> 00:03:35,002
one, the value is divided by the base. A

65
00:03:35,002 --> 00:03:39,049
negative exponent means the reciprocal: a to the power

66
00:03:39,049 --> 00:03:41,274
minus m is one over a to the power

67
00:03:41,274 --> 00:03:45,669
m. And that reciprocal is the multiplicative inverse, because

68
00:03:45,669 --> 00:03:49,263
their product is always one. Thank you for watching,

69
00:03:49,263 --> 00:03:51,380
and see you in the next lesson.
